{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:18:47Z","created_by_operation":"op_b10939b97790482c8557ec3f863024e1","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bb970ac09565e8ac5732562533f0a47501ee010c0cc8718e876c32a6f3662f2f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"microsoft/webwright@bc26750af3ad snapshot 884112d832b1b36a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5195e7f58ae4b0326df6dbb2ce0f489b9d08e3af0dc72a14c729a53cd36f6d4d","slc_62c494ea9332bcba64e6e735d447c0d40e1ad2117b19065dbe0d46163431ce20"],"source_ids":["src_21b70ef63cd25f278edb3c8aaa7227d4"],"text":"The architecture deliberately separates the agent from the browser: the browser is treated as a disposable environment the agent spawns and discards, while the persistent state is the code, screenshots, and logs in the local workspace.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:18:47Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b10939b97790482c8557ec3f863024e1"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:18:47Z","created_by_operation":"op_b10939b97790482c8557ec3f863024e1","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cab6f4036d20b0f73c54d37cf8b70e096f2104c3b6ad70cb5182f4a27bc0930d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"microsoft/webwright@bc26750af3ad snapshot 884112d832b1b36a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f0ed106130f58953a4f052b03acfea8ba6a75ff618130f90de646b98420f626","slc_50b6fe9a11829d733f4773d7a64ce0ad5363b1b58595627bc8763c280abf6a62","slc_af2a449f6210db7ec42a52efca199efa84dcb3e27e5483a95c39ab927aa69c8b"],"source_ids":["src_21b70ef63cd25f278edb3c8aaa7227d4"],"text":"A trajectory comparison viewer under assets/compare_trajectory/ (served via python3 -m http.server) accepts Webwright raw_responses.jsonl plus trajectory.json and can also display Codex and GitHub Copilot traces for token-usage comparison.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:18:47Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b10939b97790482c8557ec3f863024e1"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:18:47Z","created_by_operation":"op_b10939b97790482c8557ec3f863024e1","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e05d8da30eca9fa3a657fc33d29278d599a5fa6ed084dcb0dbd0c42b425af67b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"microsoft/webwright@bc26750af3ad snapshot 884112d832b1b36a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_200a32af5f048797df3bb05d3a225b193b0fa727919a232188707436338dc828","slc_23ce3f8077bb2dc290e9aa5addf390316eaf2386fce9c2a7ddd5d4421ddee248","slc_39a1e7f0ddedd4b835d3d55dac3a2f2b8d4e30e36adb48ce8d891bff796ab574"],"source_ids":["src_fa16ea2a863551fcafde0181cb14a1d8"],"text":"Skill Factory verification uses two gates: an input gate (gold, self_verify, or none) deciding whether a solve is trustworthy, and an output gate (strict, shape, or off) checking the distilled skill can reproduce recorded answers with no model; skills whose scripts contain every answer field verbatim are dropped as lookup-style solves.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:18:47Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b10939b97790482c8557ec3f863024e1"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:18:47Z","created_by_operation":"op_b10939b97790482c8557ec3f863024e1","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e723bcec7374a13e3f6f0708c950928feaa43d32b83dc7547e95814ca02209ef","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"microsoft/webwright@bc26750af3ad snapshot 884112d832b1b36a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5d5e171e4546eebd57218a7ec3100611d56d2b750365cf3c0e67385fcc453976"],"source_ids":["src_21b70ef63cd25f278edb3c8aaa7227d4"],"text":"Webwright gives the LLM a terminal from which it launches browser sessions to complete web tasks, capturing screenshots and page state only when needed, and each task's browsing history is captured as a single re-runnable Python script.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:18:47Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b10939b97790482c8557ec3f863024e1"}
